 {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451787} {:answer/id #uuid "7b2a906b-4563-5dbb-9794-82a69e0005c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451788}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b2a906b-4563-5dbb-9794-82a69e0005c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451788} :answer-field/id #uuid "32afa441-a36d-5b70-a78f-f611e0661706" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452741}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "87eecbfe-e80e-5243-96ba-7676172d9f04" :question/math-academy-id "q-80567" :question/problem "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed between the curve $y={x}^{2}-4$ and the $x$-axis. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}3x-y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${∬}_{D}(3x-y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,2]\\times [-4,1]$\n- **II.** ${∬}_{R}(3x-y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-4,4]$\n- **III.** ${∬}_{D}(3x-y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-4,0]$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](images/a7/a7af801fa9975dda6ce3b12b2cde2c328721cd5e0affd16f1a14ab26cfa21bdd.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}(3x-y), & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(3x-y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statements I is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement II is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statements III is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152198 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ad76e6b-acef-5221-8852-71dc42625bf3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Correct Function Used to Define a Double Integral Over a Non-Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0775b041-2fcc-5161-beb5-80cd60e4af23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474960} {:answer/id #uuid "f695d431-d46b-54df-b510-3aea6bbccfdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0775b041-2fcc-5161-beb5-80cd60e4af23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474960} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b9ce56f-633d-52a6-9fe3-5e31c2ec3104" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475406} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e2c39ea-ff23-5ab6-97b2-01c12343ec12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474962} {:answer/id #uuid "7d0dbf92-3cec-57d5-bf09-b54ff477f7e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e2c39ea-ff23-5ab6-97b2-01c12343ec12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474962} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cfbefaa-3aac-5745-9c77-f042b1776296" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475407} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "787b4942-1ca4-5050-825d-4ac096b82f5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474964} {:answer/id #uuid "b98f4c53-ec17-539a-b8eb-fcaada4b3fa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b98f4c53-ec17-539a-b8eb-fcaada4b3fa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474965} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f93c2fb-74eb-51e3-8d97-e03de7254f93" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1654ded7-c0bc-579c-a9e9-6daa6a1243e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-86894" :question/problem "![](images/5d/5d8f57afa16e99c13e6e36c5544a7c7594da13321bd3d01692a5a296a20953d7.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If $R=[-2,2]\\times [-2,2],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. $\\{\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{y}, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in D∖R\\end{aligned}$\n\nII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{y}, & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin R\\end{aligned}$\n\nIII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ x{e}^{y}, & (x,y)\\in D\\end{aligned}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D$ and the rectangle $R:$\n\n![](images/ce/ce9b9f3435a94b3f9f87b195e5b1591c80281b23cfb76ceb8e79cdeec3ae66b0.png)\n\nNotice that the rectangle $R$ contains the region $D$ completely. \n\nNow, if we define $f(x,y)$ to be equal $x{e}^{y}$ on $D$ and to be equal $0$ outside $D,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given functions.\n\n- We cannot use functions I and II. Both of these functions are not identically zero for all points in $R\\,∖D.$ For example, $(x,y)=(2,2)\\in R\\,∖\\,D,$ but the functions are nonzero at this point.\n\n- Function III equals $x{e}^{y}$ on $D$ and equals $0$ outside $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}]}
